From 09e72f9e308cc62a1f92a03259476bbb5e77780c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rafe Walker <45343084+rafe-walker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:28:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 09/19] feat(core): add auth_can_i (C13)

There was no way to ask whether an action is permitted. On the native
session (job 9) the agent tried to create a SubjectAccessReview through
resources_create_or_update ("cannot patch subjectaccessreviews": the
apply tool can only patch) and spent 4,323 tokens and an error to learn
what `kubectl auth can-i` answers in one line.

auth_can_i(verb, apiVersion+kind | resource+group, subresource,
namespace, name, user, groups) creates a SelfSubjectAccessReview for
the server's own identity, or with `user` a SubjectAccessReview for
another subject (which needs permission to create those; a refusal is
returned as an error). The answer is one line ("yes: this server's
identity may create networkpolicies.networking.k8s.io in namespace
shop", or "no: ... may not ..." with the authorizer's reason), plus the
same as structured content. A kind is resolved to its resource through
discovery; for a cluster-scoped kind the namespace is dropped.

Annotated read-only (an access review is answered, not stored),
idempotent, open world.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
